# scripts/install/maintainer.gpg - LivOS release maintainer PUBLIC keyring
# (Phase 311-04, UPDSAFE-02)
#
# WARNING: PLACEHOLDER - NON-FUNCTIONAL. This is NOT a real maintainer public key.
# The build environment could not run gpg key generation (gpg-agent unavailable),
# so a clearly-marked placeholder ASCII-armored public keyring is shipped.
#
# The operator MUST replace this file with a real exported PUBLIC key BEFORE the
# Phase 311 release tag is cut. Off-repo key-gen + export ceremony:
#     gpg --batch --quick-gen-key "LivOS Maintainer <maintainer@livinity.io>" \n#         ed25519 sign never          # private key stays OFF-REPO (operator-held)
#     gpg --armor --export <keyid> > scripts/install/maintainer.gpg   # PUBLIC only
#   Commit ONLY the ASCII-armored public keyring. The private half is retained
#   off-repo by the operator for future  git tag -s  signing (a follow-up ceremony,
#   NOT done in Phase 311). NEVER commit the private key half to the repo.
#
# WARN-ONLY / priority note: livos_verify_fetched_ref() resolves EXPECTED_RELEASE
# (pin-file, path b) BEFORE this maintainer.gpg (verify-tag, path c). During the
# Phase 311 warn-only cycle the pin file resolves first, so this GPG verify-tag
# path is intentionally UNEXERCISED - Phase 312 must plan for zero GPG-path
# telemetry. A mismatch here is WARN-ONLY in Phase 311 (never aborts); fail-closed
# is Phase 312 (a later release).
#
